    "body": "Sounds good. I guess one interesting thing is that this paragraph says we cannot use \"global\" objects while in parallel, while we clearly agree that we actually make an exception for globals, since that's the only way we can schedule things _back_ on the main thread. In other words, we are assuming https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6475#issuecomment-796587434 to be true—that most accesses to a global, especially when scheduling tasks, are atomic. That's the right assumption make IMO. I'm just trying to think if we should state this assumption/exception clearly in this paragraph too.",
